---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import CommandBlock from "../components/CommandBlock.astro";
import ManifestPanel from "../components/ManifestPanel.astro";
import SafetyNotice from "../components/SafetyNotice.astro";
import SignalCard from "../components/SignalCard.astro";

const installCommand = "curl -fsSL https://arkheionx.dev/install | bash";
---

<Layout
  title="ArkheionX | Deterministic review artifacts"
  description="Local-first infrastructure for mapping Solidity and Foundry repositories into reproducible review surfaces."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner page-shell">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="page-kicker">Local security review infrastructure</p>
        <h1>ArkheionX</h1>
        <p class="hero-tagline">Deterministic review artifacts for human security researchers.</p>
        <p class="hero-summary">
          Local-first infrastructure for mapping Solidity / Foundry repositories into reviewable protocol surfaces:
          roles, value paths, assumptions, test gaps, evidence links, and fixture benchmark snapshots.
        </p>
        <CommandBlock title="install / main" command={installCommand} />
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs">Read the docs</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/Yudis-bit/DeFi-Exploit-PoCs">View GitHub</a>
        </div>
        <div class="status-strip" aria-label="Operating boundaries">
          <span>LOCAL-FIRST</span>
          <span>NO RPC BY DEFAULT</span>
          <span>NO EXPLOIT AUTOMATION</span>
          <span>HUMAN REVIEW REQUIRED</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ManifestPanel />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow amber">Review surface</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Review context without scanner noise.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <p>ArkheionX focuses on reproducible review context, not automatic vulnerability claims.</p>
          <p>
            A review starts with structure: which contracts hold authority, where value enters and exits, which
            assumptions connect components, and where test evidence is absent. ArkheionX records that surface in
            inspectable local artifacts so a researcher can trace, question, and regenerate it.
          </p>
          <p>
            The output is a map for investigation. It is not a verdict, a score to trust without inspection, or a
            substitute for protocol-specific reasoning.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow blue">Artifact inventory</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">What the machine preserves.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Stable identifiers and bounded local evidence make review state easier to compare across commits, machines,
        and researchers.
      </p>
      <div class="signal-grid">
        <SignalCard index="01" title="Protocol roles" tone="green">Contract and function roles that orient manual inspection.</SignalCard>
        <SignalCard index="02" title="Value paths" tone="blue">Candidate flows across deposits, accounting, transfers, and exits.</SignalCard>
        <SignalCard index="03" title="Assumptions" tone="amber">Explicit trust and state conditions that need researcher verification.</SignalCard>
        <SignalCard index="04" title="Test gaps" tone="amber">Missing local evidence attached to specific protocol surfaces.</SignalCard>
        <SignalCard index="05" title="Evidence links" tone="blue">Cross-references between targets and generated local artifacts.</SignalCard>
        <SignalCard index="06" title="Fixture benchmarks" tone="green">Repeatable checks over nine controlled local/static protocol shapes.</SignalCard>
        <SignalCard index="07" title="Source fingerprints" tone="blue">SHA-256 fingerprints for the exact fixture source bytes inspected.</SignalCard>
        <SignalCard index="08" title="Snapshot drift" tone="amber">Visible changes when deterministic benchmark output moves.</SignalCard>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="split-band">
    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow green">Default posture</p>
      <h2>Local-first by design.</h2>
      <p>
        The standard workflow reads an authorized repository on your machine. It requires no RPC endpoint, deployed
        target, account credential, or hosted service.
      </p>
      <ul class="evidence-list">
        <li><span>NET/00</span><span>Repository files</span><span>LOCAL</span></li>
        <li><span>RPC/00</span><span>Network calls</span><span>OFF</span></li>
        <li><span>KEY/00</span><span>Secret material</span><span>NONE</span></li>
        <li><span>TX/00</span><span>Transaction broadcast</span><span>NONE</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section>
      <p class="eyebrow blue">Benchmark layer</p>
      <h2>Fixture benchmark harness.</h2>
      <p>
        Nine small, controlled Solidity-like fixtures exercise deterministic IDs, JSON serialization, path safety,
        source fingerprints, snapshot stability, and safety-boundary checks.
      </p>
      <p>
        Fixtures are static inputs. The harness does not compile them, execute them, or treat a passing snapshot as
        evidence that a protocol is secure.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/docs/fixture-harness">Inspect the fixture model</a>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <SafetyNotice>
        <p>
          A machine-generated role, path, gap, or evidence state can prioritize investigation. Impact,
          exploitability, and severity remain decisions for an authorized human reviewer working from the source and
          supporting evidence.
        </p>
      </SafetyNotice>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="section-inner quickstart-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow green">Five commands</p>
        <h2 class="section-title">Establish a local review surface.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">Check the install, inspect a bundled demo, then map an authorized repository.</p>
        <div class="inline-actions">
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/quickstart">Quickstart details</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/docs/cli-reference">CLI reference</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <CommandBlock
        title="review session"
        command={`arkheionx version
arkheionx doctor
arkheionx demo
arkheionx scan .
arkheionx review-map .`}
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow amber">Distribution state</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">Public artifact status.</h2>
      <div class="artifact-status">
        <div><span>Source</span><strong>v3.9.0 public-safe state</strong></div>
        <div><span>Binary releases</span><strong>Not yet published</strong></div>
        <div><span>Installer</span><strong>Source install from GitHub main</strong></div>
        <div><span>License</span><strong>Pending maintainer decision</strong></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
